    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0899" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.6431/10–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Representative in Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-13T14:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>534. Reurtels 714 Oct 5 and 719 Oct 6, Deptel 536 Oct. 13.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d832-f1"/> Dept, thinks it would be inadvisable for you to indicate
                    to Hungarians any support for refusal to ratify economic collaboration
                    agreement, US cannot of course assume responsibility independently to make up
                    economic losses Hungary might suffer as a result of Soviet reprisals or make
                    commitments at this time to supply goods, capital or technical aid which are
                    provided for by Soviet-Hungarian agreement.</p>
                <p>If Hungarian officials should approach you again, it would be preferable not to
                    go beyond general statements you have already made.</p>
                <p>Telegram will follow<anchor n="12" xml:id="d832-f2"/> giving Dept. views on
                    relation to present situation of US-Hungarian treaty of friendship commerce and
                    consular rights of 1926.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d832-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d832-f1" n="11" xml:id="d832-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 536, October 13, to Budapest, same as telegram 2159, October 13, to
                    Moscow, <ref target="#pg888">p. 888</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d832-f2" n="12" xml:id="d832-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 590, October 26, 8 p.m., to Budapest, <ref target="#pg899">p.
                    899</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d832-f3" n="13" xml:id="d832-f3-content">
                <p>Treaty signed June 24, 1925 (ratifications exchanged September 4, 1926),, <ref
                        target="frus1925v02#pg_341">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1925, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 341</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
